AC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787511358553764001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"## Context\n\n`docs/architecture.md` describes RP-04 as unimplemented, and `docs/reuse-surface.md` says its diagnostic shadow will be removed in S7. RP-04 is closed. `REBAR_OPERATION_SNAPSHOT_SHADOW` remains enabled by default and diagnostic only for legacy shadow surfaces. Ticket vibrant-legal-hind, ADR 0098, and ticket opal-daffy-mutt establish this qualified current state.\n\n## Plan\n\n- Describe the implemented `OperationSnapshot` composer and runtime bindings.\n- Describe provider authentication carriers and the configuration ownership gate.\n- Identify the remaining diagnostic-only shadow boundary.\n- Avoid claiming that the snapshot controls every operation.\n- Remove migration-pending wording that RP-04 completion superseded.\n- Preserve ADR 0098 as a historical decision record and leave runtime behavior unchanged.\n- Run documentation links, reuse-surface contracts, and focused operation-snapshot tests.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Architecture documentation identifies RP-04 as implemented.\n- [ ] The documented current boundary includes composition, runtime binding, authentication carriers, and ownership enforcement.\n- [ ] The remaining diagnostic shadow is described as diagnostic only and enabled by default.\n- [ ] The documentation does not claim universal operation control.\n- [ ] ADR 0098 and runtime behavior remain unchanged.\n- [ ] Focused documentation and operation-snapshot checks pass.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"docs/architecture.md","reason":"Replace stale RP-04 migration status with the qualified implemented boundary."},{"path":"docs/reuse-surface.md","reason":"Correct the current O